  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>“You hear this music? That means it’s time for me to bust some heads”</p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Charisma 15, character level 5, either Power Attack or Dodge.</p>\n<p><strong>Benefit:</strong> You gain the ability to emit a personal theme song, creating music you find enjoyable as a standard action. This song acts as a supernatural ghost sound, lasting a number of rounds equal to your character level. You may do this a number of times per day equal to 1 + your Charisma modifier. While your personal theme song is active, you gain a benefit based on the feat you used to qualify for this feat. If you qualified using Power Attack, you receive a +2 morale bonus on attack and damage rolls (even if not using Power Attack). If you qualified using Dodge, you receive a +2 morale bonus to AC and saves.</p>\n<p><strong>Special:</strong> If you qualify for this feat with both prerequisites, you may gain either benefit, and swap between the benefits as a free action at the start of your turn. Henshin heroes, magical girls, and others characters with a transformation trinket can activate their personal theme song as a free action on the turn they use their transformation ability.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/gonzo-feats#toc38\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
